#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171890 :question/id #uuid "8f9615ef-b53e-51ee-9aa6-4df88afd6773" :question/math-academy-id "e-9441" :question/problem "![](images/29/2966d95bee0326ed5bf5a5fec9313d15bacd86334f9e9d144ff366bee63d9de3.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\n- $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}$\n\n- $\\mathbf G(x,y) = 2 \\, \\mathbf{i}$\n\n- $\\mathbf H(x,y) = -x \\, \\mathbf{i}$" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $\\mathbf j$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' horizontal components (i.e., the $\\mathbf i$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf G(x,y) = 2 \\, \\mathbf{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $\\mathbf{H}(x,y) = -x\\, \\mathbf{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171894 :question/id #uuid "b226c391-9538-59ff-85ff-dde4d73f209b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9473" :question/problem "![](images/de/de305db47bcfae58b75797e88ae4a7c7825174bd58d77991ba8dfb4c0b8a13cb.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\n- $\\mathbf  F(x,y,z) = \\mathbf j + \\mathbf k$\n\n- $\\mathbf  G(x,y,z) = \\mathbf k$\n\n- $\\mathbf  H(x,y,z) = z\\,\\mathbf k$\n\n- $\\mathbf  K(x,y,z) = -\\mathbf k$" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $z$-axis. So, the $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z) = \\mathbf j + \\mathbf k\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $z$-direction, so the $\\mathbf k$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf G(x,y,z) = \\mathbf k\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $\\mathbf i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf H(x,y,z) = z\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $\\mathbf K(x,y,z) = -\\mathbf k.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171897 :question/id #uuid "fb87998f-3236-510b-94aa-7db80487d8c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9498" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92a7327-4920-5e27-9447-1c7bf838154d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/17/17e2a819903c4836cbf77cd117939be363525a6483082cede15ea73108231d46.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168514} {:answer/id #uuid "e17373c4-5676-5b64-994a-a014b8fd8b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/63/63543b3fb37cc73765bcd65d0bbbd575911bd672aa4f15b90ade19f4182b660e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168515} {:answer/id #uuid "1d55af91-f6ba-5a1e-8faf-0fe5df83e992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/54/54e21214507a8882e2b19130a8266c39a1b92252d54ae7ae4015a9494fce52a2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168516} {:answer/id #uuid "1e741758-8137-51f7-8727-2cfad442752f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a2/a25f4c185e44773e8689785e04dc8d3c70a9934e8e02eee94a5c85061eebfd52.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168517} {:answer/id #uuid "64618133-3b91-5a3a-ada3-c2b6802ed1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f0/f074ea082192f9d653f8519f79dc05fb7c732f6c695444b167ce2417844b6a36.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168518}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7d2410-bf2a-5ecd-956a-96e998dbd0fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168513}] :question/id #uuid "19719bc2-a844-5b6e-926d-79b5bdfa6933" :question/math-academy-id "q-122264" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x, y) = x^{2}i - 2yj$ at the indicated points?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9798dcb4-1378-51aa-94b5-6f2b05c5a513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x, y) = xi - j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168520} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ab7585-cdb1-5031-b00c-6bd7293fb822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x, y) = i + 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168521} {:answer/id #uuid "74fe15fc-2329-5341-9f1b-ca6399a41099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x, y) =-xi + yj" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168522} {:answer/id #uuid "77138ede-65f3-5aa8-859e-7ba94c5edf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168523} {:answer/id #uuid "79114562-ae7e-51b9-8192-e814accd7704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x, y) = i - 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168524}] :answer-field/id #uuid "69c09b2e-0e0e-5814-9b8e-43892aa92ebf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168519}] :question/id #uuid "561ee574-102b-5192-93c3-2aebaaee05b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-122296" :question/problem "![](images/14/14a67562652c609deeaf6b7606cee130685e2c2b5382f1a5436cd4e441591b94.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05602332-e37c-5460-b172-b751e231ce9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y)=i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253707} {:answer/id #uuid "22a9c2bb-60e1-58e5-9874-7cbd061245fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253982} {:answer/id #uuid "975ec189-e7bf-53b5-bbdd-1f4be9ecf1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255004} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d17860-5ab2-534f-9821-dacba55fba0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255244} {:answer/id #uuid "c9697585-eb9c-571c-9a60-d1c3239f7491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255461}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253982} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff26018b-9fd9-5c42-b4cb-d605e4c4ebfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b0d06ed-9894-556b-a427-a46e4623bd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-122463" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3614ea1954f36435eb1ab5f52c04d4fa3062ac337eccf76a5b47e4a03a64a1b.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i-2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-i+j.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0af393b5-0b0a-51ee-963e-9232b624b8d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253755} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebe45a6-6f14-5783-a2c5-0fff74a623ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)={e}^{x}\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254352} {:answer/id #uuid "5a235ec0-b137-57da-bcd7-fa7e7f95a670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=i+j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254460} {:answer/id #uuid "6c27c496-3691-52cb-89b6-a510f5ec6427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254631} {:answer/id #uuid "99ad8cef-0db5-5109-bbb4-eb38f07c8dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255028}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186254631} :answer-field/id #uuid "1226930a-6b24-57fb-a5e7-1829039d9728" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "505eb075-afb5-5225-b846-447773bcc89d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122559" :question/problem "![](images/cf/cfc15b6202167211b7d6c0e8f6635dd9e571810d5296a209a4c317350604c4a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=i+j+k,\\,\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)={e}^{x}\\,i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $F(x,y,z)=i.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f0b5a2-3be5-594f-a754-99c98d96988e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254295} {:answer/id #uuid "c4981513-4d32-54f0-884a-7cfa95b9c2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255427} {:answer/id #uuid "d6dc3e8c-9e7f-50a4-b937-a99d9f06d7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=i-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255572} {:answer/id #uuid "da52d501-6db0-512c-804d-9bbd6ce2ad8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255607} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbc53f3-143a-5ed2-b73c-2af527f6a4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "K(x,y,z)=2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255881} :answer-field/id #uuid "a548685d-413d-5f58-8841-0b64dd56f823" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0777fbfe-65b4-5afe-92ce-361fbbf5b37f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122664" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7a0a919af689e9c332ba6ceb3d606208dab9eabadef9b4871ac8e164843ebe88.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $z$-axis. So, the $i$ and $j$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=i-k\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $z$-direction, so the $k$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=-k\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $k$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y,z)=2\\,k.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0a4588a-a70a-5752-b2c8-01cc42d39edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/27/271bcaebb02bc573b2d6c3b00758387ff1a49787270c137f7e69ed3223e7de2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168580} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb7e952-7f56-56d6-875d-d7fd08e13aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/33/33c6c3680f3cab38ffd1508fad160948f3bc1159c01dc287b3fe113c0cf89875.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168581} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0e3626-c59b-53de-817d-5c6c8128a918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/21/21fc0f3e9a2d5100421953ef2270de9d8a99fb395d761b4eb9a3f9f0e1889ac3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168582} {:answer/id #uuid "7951f9ae-9706-5dfa-82a5-3cfe79b73cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4d/4d3b3c7f1a3b85e40cec4392b4c487c5423636837ea2672c6cdcd6fdeb2b0cc7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168583} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0edf41-9f7f-55ea-993a-529370820e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1f/1f87c6b14dba3adad00c49362df7ba03bcbb6f990eba0302bcd10d484f15b070.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168584}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d97d5ed5-35ab-5c3c-88ac-a04ef2adefb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f19d19af-b717-5081-be6e-62e25a75c568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4d/4d3b3c7f1a3b85e40cec4392b4c487c5423636837ea2672c6cdcd6fdeb2b0cc7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380707} {:answer/id #uuid "b54cebe4-6aa6-502d-9b98-b267d3c2bb70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/33/33c6c3680f3cab38ffd1508fad160948f3bc1159c01dc287b3fe113c0cf89875.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380708} {:answer/id #uuid "480fd893-6a75-5704-903f-fe9945ae2257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/27/271bcaebb02bc573b2d6c3b00758387ff1a49787270c137f7e69ed3223e7de2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380709} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e4571a-7acf-5877-a904-62367ce6ac1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1f/1f87c6b14dba3adad00c49362df7ba03bcbb6f990eba0302bcd10d484f15b070.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380710} {:answer/id #uuid "e08cd2a9-0dc9-5455-b4d2-241cc812bcb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/21/21fc0f3e9a2d5100421953ef2270de9d8a99fb395d761b4eb9a3f9f0e1889ac3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380708} :answer-field/id #uuid "08090d20-3972-5c5d-a3b3-2558a12e085f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "59a69c0f-c2af-5b88-9b38-1fbc42cfdc3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122756" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi y}{2}\\right)\\,j\n$$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-3,1),(-2,-1),$ and $(4,-4).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $$\n\\displaystyle F(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{2}\\,j:\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-3,1) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (-3))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{2}\\right)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(-2,-1) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (-2))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi (-1)}{2}\\right)\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(4,-4) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (4))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi (-4)}{2}\\right)\\,j=2\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/33/33c6c3680f3cab38ffd1508fad160948f3bc1159c01dc287b3fe113c0cf89875.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aec1b3a-f253-5279-99f6-12a688430707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168610} {:answer/id #uuid "acbd015f-0d6c-538b-9f05-45ee71f8c513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168611} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e6ebd5-405c-535f-9ceb-b01c692d8bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168612} {:answer/id #uuid "53f9ce92-f40b-51c9-86f1-dceb0bbaeb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168613} {:answer/id #uuid "76624ec5-45cd-5b6f-a504-2ff12623de24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168614}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168613} :answer-field/id #uuid "2431be4b-89af-5247-a309-422a67c531ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8379be09-e532-538d-bf76-16e36177bb9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123890" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (1,1)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,2x-y\\ne 0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(1,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a4aa1b-5437-5440-884c-81fec8a3e35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168616} {:answer/id #uuid "cbaa7d9a-d85e-56eb-bd20-9f2355eceaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168617} {:answer/id #uuid "062d51b9-4b55-58f7-add6-c3af62507b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168618} {:answer/id #uuid "0c00036a-af38-55db-b1fa-35ac03e1fc7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168619} {:answer/id #uuid "248e5e90-03a0-57d7-b164-39fd663dcbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168620}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5f0887-2a07-5db9-bd00-e689f95cdb12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6803c79e-d9ef-543b-9ca8-b54f706cd2da" :question/math-academy-id "q-123920" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n1. ${(x, y) ∈ R^{2} \\mid 4x^{2} + y^{2} \\le 4}$\n2. ${(x, y) ∈ R^{2} \\mid y - x \\ne 0}$\n3. $R^{2}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6491ad-31df-5c44-8510-45289f4f4d41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{u+v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401201} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2a58c0-318a-559b-8de4-48cf1599122b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401202} {:answer/id #uuid "66a3fc66-6953-52e2-8b17-93c3ff13ddf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "uv\\sqrt{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401203} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fed922-03a1-59c5-b2d8-bcf5a4514733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "uv\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401204} {:answer/id #uuid "ecef412c-1fbd-55f7-a2eb-dcc4e3d8418d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401205}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401205} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5472ad-00ad-5af8-bfaf-97021ee46355" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "25e44fde-444d-5880-ba2e-43dd4bc039db" :question/math-academy-id "q-160711" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xyz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & v \\\\ 1 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-v)^{2}+(-u)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xyz)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =u\\cdot v\\cdot uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6318e5-3878-5d26-b61b-739d349729a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} {:answer/id #uuid "2913e3a7-4834-5ae0-8725-8cf0ddd19bbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+uv+{u}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275848} {:answer/id #uuid "4635f4d0-2e93-54c6-a194-c7414540fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276098} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7629cd-993c-5b5b-a5b5-4827bb2f0380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276769} {:answer/id #uuid "fa861672-33f6-547e-b490-0aa338df3abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(u+v)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277670}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} :answer-field/id #uuid "758915d5-fc00-56c4-ac7b-2a8b40d5ac5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a99cdea7-3ae5-5a3e-abca-eaac3de706cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-160712" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+y+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=u-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+(u-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11345332-1583-5403-b382-1f7db9544110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414431} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed83581-5e32-5a0e-8a25-178bb99cade4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414439} {:answer/id #uuid "7d00c43b-e899-573d-afa8-6b12ead91cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414440} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8100ab-c718-514d-8f3c-f28643c256a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414447} {:answer/id #uuid "d24b3aff-8b91-5bf0-8ab1-f276e0780c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414450}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414440} :answer-field/id #uuid "be382d30-f02e-5329-bcf7-16808280a34b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "82d5af65-9d79-5b70-b0f6-be91c0743951" :question/math-academy-id "q-160834" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}(2x+y+z)\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-v,\\,3u+2,\\,u+2v⟩\n$$\n\n \nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{70}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{70}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(2x+y+z)\\,{|}_{x=2u-v\\,y=3u+2\\,z=u+2v} \\\\  & =2(2u-v)+(3u+2)+(u+2v) \\\\  & =8u+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(8u+2)\\sqrt{70}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{∬}_{D}\\,(8u+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8u+2)\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot [4{u}^{2}+2u]_{0}^{1}\\cdot [u]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{70}\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a1c5c4-aaff-5dad-85ae-7c455c4e77b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169132} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5264d6-51e2-571c-a97d-f200747b780d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169133} {:answer/id #uuid "d262b1ed-6abf-5731-aad7-a59edbd4996a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169134} {:answer/id #uuid "033ce6a7-bfa6-5c47-acc2-cddc0cab717e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169135} {:answer/id #uuid "2814803c-3a0a-59a5-b8f2-9a2b1d57c431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186169133} :answer-field/id #uuid "126dc10e-27a9-5d7d-894d-84b3d2d7de05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "588db1ad-67d5-5fad-b786-e13158fbed5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160835" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=6-3u-2v\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,6-3u-2v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(6-3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3,\\,2,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =4xy\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=6-3u-2v} \\\\  & =4uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we denote \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\},\n$$\n\nour surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}4xy\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{∬}_{D}\\,4uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2u\\,\\text{d}u\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}2v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot [{u}^{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [{v}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot 4\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =36\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f09971ee-e0b1-5368-b43f-c0ddce3cf5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/46/46c8f0a1fc890eec1ba1c7d907bd1fb614a52c114d3d1c4e75d75cc786bb7e34.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171622} {:answer/id #uuid "f3fdf4cf-d194-5a0e-bf0f-f714f390c8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/71/71b2e8c4e0a756b57e61ad3bfacb99bfca2ee36ffa6488c2fd143cea8505b6e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171623} {:answer/id #uuid "2a83c0a3-26bc-5b40-851b-313168b9c6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ee/ee2785963eb39186c88249abeb8b5aea1c5d95e6631cf38edc7476a696866e06.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171624} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1e9073-fa5f-5949-a5f2-ec63cafa0632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/12/1221e9c3a65a52d807be6e32fcea3949a8c49a8f8cf55a365e1b452bf381fb94.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171625} {:answer/id #uuid "7b7bd01c-ef6b-58e9-a50a-b357226fb10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e4/e41d6db9c694177af290dd9c0414aefe0559f956c129612457a1d4a9312fb686.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171626}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9dba4603-85b6-5c93-905c-c5a0334b6448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d490908f-429a-57f1-9368-ba4a54eb6caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ee/ee2785963eb39186c88249abeb8b5aea1c5d95e6631cf38edc7476a696866e06.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395385} {:answer/id #uuid "310ce816-620b-570e-9b09-6936220dfbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/12/1221e9c3a65a52d807be6e32fcea3949a8c49a8f8cf55a365e1b452bf381fb94.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395386} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc11e65-ac34-5015-a488-896c5641d1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/71/71b2e8c4e0a756b57e61ad3bfacb99bfca2ee36ffa6488c2fd143cea8505b6e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395387} {:answer/id #uuid "382d591f-1979-54c5-9b11-63bfd90933dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e4/e41d6db9c694177af290dd9c0414aefe0559f956c129612457a1d4a9312fb686.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395388} {:answer/id #uuid "fde4099f-25c8-5fc5-94ac-5a41589b0f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/46/46c8f0a1fc890eec1ba1c7d907bd1fb614a52c114d3d1c4e75d75cc786bb7e34.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395389}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395385} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9cef5d8-3343-5724-9f71-6c55d32d97b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e05dacf-ca5c-5d30-8870-e69c9a92d503" :question/math-academy-id "q-98032" :question/problem "Which of the following regions is connected?" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/0b/0baa675c757282d73c238ab1e81ef7ed252945a95098841bbf52b9f558d693c2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1dc695-98aa-599a-ad75-58ff2c4dd03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/83/830bd2d62b3473f536e0c985d3c6eaab7c3b004617ecef95d9b5d7786d8e8298.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361247} {:answer/id #uuid "98422db7-d266-5534-87b0-03c11acd352b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bb/bb7e27b487ebf34772cf82f7a2f5cc7c6d310a59066e807bce3a236d